WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.032
Decoder-only models are organized around next-token prediction.

00:00:04.032 --> 00:00:11.532
Given the tokens generated or provided so far, the model predicts a probability distribution for the next

00:00:11.532 --> 00:00:17.247
token. After one token is chosen, it is appended to the sequence and the process repeats.

00:00:17.247 --> 00:00:22.552
That simple training objective scales into text completion, instruction following, code generation,

00:00:22.552 --> 00:00:27.887
and chat when the model is trained and tuned appropriately.

00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:28.582
GPT-style architectures are decoder-only.

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:36.232
Their self-attention is causal, meaning a position cannot use information from future tokens during

00:00:36.232 --> 00:00:42.862
generation. The model can only condition on the prefix that is already available.

00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:47.117
This is exactly what we need when generating text from left to right.

00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:49.762
Decoder-only models can also analyze provided context,

00:00:49.762 --> 00:00:55.403
but their architecture and training objective make generation their natural strength.
